# Microsoft Secure Boot certificate set
#
# Republished byte-for-byte from Microsoft's own publication URLs below. These
# are PUBLIC certificates that Microsoft publishes precisely so that platform
# owners can enrol them; Debian, Fedora, sbctl and efitools all redistribute
# them the same way. No private key is involved and nothing here is secret.
#
# Verify any file by downloading the source URL and comparing sha256.
#
# WHY FOG SHIPS THESE AT ALL
#
# The automated enrolment path (docs/adr/0008, fos docs/adr/0009) replaces the
# platform key, which means FOG decides what else stays trusted. The decisive
# entry is "Microsoft Corporation UEFI CA 2011": it signs the shim in FOG's OWN
# boot chain --
#
#     secureboot/snponly-shimx64.efi -> secureboot/snponly.efi -> FOS kernel
#
# -- so a db without it does not merely break Windows, it breaks FOG's Secure
# Boot PXE boot. We would enrol our key and destroy the thing we enrolled it
# for. The Windows PCA entries are what keep the client's installed OS bootable.
#
# The 2023 generation is included because it is what new hardware and newly
# signed binaries are moving to; enrolling only the 2011 set would work today
# and quietly stop working on newer machines.
#
# Fetched 2026-08-03. All files are DER.
